  "result": "Perfect! All 358 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the `mergeCustomers` function with complete test coverage. Here's what was added:\n\n## Changes\n\n**src/errors.js**\n- Added `SAME_CUSTOMER` error code for when both IDs are the same customer\n\n**src/customers.js**\n- Added `mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)` function that:\n  - Normalizes both customer IDs\n  - Returns `SAME_CUSTOMER` error if both IDs are identical\n  - Returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` if either customer doesn't exist\n  - Removes the `fromId` customer from the array\n  - Updates all invoices belonging to `fromId` to belong to `intoId`\n  - Returns `ok({ customers, invoices })` with the merged results\n  - Doesn't mutate the original arrays\n\n**test/customers.test.js**\n- Added 7 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Successful merge removing fromId and keeping intoId\n  - Invoice transfer from one customer to another\n  - CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND when fromId doesn't exist\n  - CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND when intoId doesn't exist\n  - SAME_CUSTOMER error handling\n  - ID normalization (whitespace and case insensitivity)\n  - Original arrays are not mutated\n\nAll tests pass, and no existing tests were broken.",
